// MetaTagHealthReport thresholds for a triple-quoted meta-tag value, e.g. { Description = ... }.
// MEASURED against df-cli 1.0.0 (DF 26 GA) on 2026-08-23 by compiling generated probes: a block of
// 2216 characters compiles and 2217 does not. Over the limit the compiler does not report an error
// - it dies with an access violation, so the build prints "Rebuilding X ..." and then NOTHING, exits
// 0, and leaves a ZERO-BYTE .err file. CI_MetaTagCrashChars is that measured cliff (2 characters of
// slack); CI_MetaTagMaxSafeChars is the budget we ask maintainers to stay inside so that adding one
// more sub-tag later cannot push a function over. Re-measure when the DataFlex major version changes.
// Full rules: the header comment of oRefactorFuncLib.pkg.
Define CI_MetaTagMaxSafeChars       for 2000

Define CI_MetaTagCrashChars         for 2215

// Obsolete packages the DataFlex compiler flags 4536 as "obsolete ... can be removed / just comment
// out the Use statement" - a PURE removal (their functionality is now in FMAC / the runtime, so no
// code breaks). CommentOutObsoletePackageUse comments out 'Use <one-of-these>'. LOWERCASE basenames,
// comma-separated (matched case-insensitively). Only genuinely-removable packages belong here - NOT
// the "Use cX class instead" ones (those need a code change, not a removal), and NOT func.pkg (its
// functions have alternatives that must be adopted first). (Nils 2026-07-09: Case.mac - Case is in FMAC.)
Define CS_RemovableObsoletePackages for "case.mac,dfbase.pkg,winbase.pkg,destobj.pkg,dfcmbfrm.pkg,dfradio.pkg,dflblmx.pkg,dftabdg.pkg"

