/* HTML ENTITIES BY NAME (Nils 2026-08-25) - CS_EmDash, CS_MidDot, CS_Nbsp, CS_Ellipsis, CS_Check, CS_RArrow,
   CS_Times, CS_Bullet, and CS_WarnSign, CS_PlayTriangle, CS_UpTriangle, CS_DownTriangle - are Library-RDCFlexTron's
   own (FTConstants.h.pkg) since DFRefactor's pin moved to 0.9.1 (2026-09-29), as are CS_NlEntity, CS_AposEntity
   and the whole tags (CS_DivOpen, CS_DivEnd, CS_SpanOpen, CS_SpanEnd, CS_ParaOpen, CS_ParaEnd, CS_Br). */
/* THE GLYPHS, BY WHAT THEY MEAN (Nils 2026-08-25: "Can you tell me what the #9888 is?").

   A numeric character reference is a character written by its decimal codepoint, so the file can
   stay single-byte. It also tells the reader nothing: &#9888; is a warning triangle and &#10697;
   is the glyph on the version row, and no amount of staring at the number says so. The generic ones
   (CS_WarnSign and the triangles) are Library-RDCFlexTron's now; these are the Libraries dialog's.

   THE VARIATION SELECTOR IS FOLDED IN. &#65038; (U+FE0E) is not a character - it forces the glyph
   before it to render as monochrome TEXT rather than as a colour emoji. Three of these need it and
   were written as a pair at every call site, which is a pairing to get wrong. It lives in the
   constant now, so a caller cannot separate them. */
Define CS_LicenceGlyph              for "&#9878;&#65038;"    // U+2696 scales - the Libraries licence row
Define CS_GearGlyph                 for "&#9881;&#65038;"    // U+2699 gear - the DataFlex versions row
Define CS_PublisherGlyph            for "&#128100;&#65038;"  // U+1F464 bust - the publisher row
Define CS_VersionGlyph              for "&#10697;"           // U+29C9 two joined squares - the version row
Define CS_CommitGlyph               for "&#9673;"            // U+25C9 fisheye - a pinned git commit
Define CS_RequiresGlyph             for "&#8618;"            // U+21AA hooked arrow - "brings these with it"

/* THE CLICK IDS THAT CROSS A FILE BOUNDARY (2026-08-25).

   A data-ServerOnClick id is a contract between the markup that emits it and the OnClick that
   answers it. Where both halves sit in one file, the literal is fine - the two are a screen apart
   and a typo shows the moment you click. These ten do NOT: the shared tile builders emit them and
   the boards answer them, so a typo in either half is a button that does nothing, with no error
   anywhere and nothing in a log.

   Named where the id is ONE user action wherever it appears - "compare" opens the same comparison
   whichever screen offers it, so BackupFilesFT and EditorViewFT share the constant even though
   each also answers its own button.

   NOT named: the same word used for something else. FTDashIcons selects a glyph with
   If (sName = "compare"), which is a different thing that happens to be spelled alike, and it keeps
   its literal. The rule is the contract, not the spelling - only a data-ServerOnClick id and the
   OnClick that answers it are substituted here. */
Define CS_IdCompare                 for "compare"        // cFTTileMarkup   -> the boards
Define CS_IdHistory                 for "history"        // cFTTileMarkup   -> DashboardFT
Define CS_IdReadLog                 for "readlog"        // cFTTileMarkup   -> both boards
Define CS_IdReadOtherLogs           for "readotherlogs"  // cFTTileMarkup   -> both boards
Define CS_IdSetup                   for "setup"          // cFTTileMarkup   -> both boards
Define CS_IdUndo                    for "undo"           // cFTTileMarkup   -> both boards
Define CS_IdFnLib                   for "fnlib"          // cFTTileMarkup   -> ManualDashboard, StartCenter
Define CS_IdSelFolders              for "folders"        // cFTManualBoard  -> ManualDashboard, CmdLineIniFileExporter
Define CS_IdSelFunctions            for "functions"      // cFTManualBoard  -> ManualDashboard, CmdLineIniFileExporter
Define CS_IdSelFile                 for "file"           // cFTManualBoard  -> ManualDashboard
Define CS_IdScanFile                for "scanfile"       // cFTManualBoard  -> ManualDashboard (single-file mode: Analyze this file)

/* DFREFACTOR'S OWN GLYPHS (2026-09-29, the RDCFlexTron pin move to 0.9.1): SVG files in AppHtml\FTGlyphs, which
   the library's FTAppGlyphs.pkg reads when the program starts (SeedFTAppGlyphs, FTThemeSeed.pkg) and draws like its
   own CS_Glyph* glyphs - by DashIcon, IconLabel and the ftg- classes. The file name is the glyph's name.

   They replace the CS_Ico* names, the stems of the <img> files in AppHtml\Svg (removed) that IconLabel drew until 0.9.0 - in
   the one fixed grey they were drawn in, barely there on the light theme. Every other icon of that set is a library
   glyph that draws the same thing: Close and Cancel the x of CS_GlyphClose, Proceed the tick of CS_GlyphCheck,
   Clear CS_GlyphEraser, Rescan CS_GlyphRefresh, Scan CS_GlyphScan, Plan CS_GlyphPlan, and the selection four
   CS_GlyphSelectAll, CS_GlyphSelectNone, CS_GlyphInvert and CS_GlyphHierarchy. These six are DFRefactor's own.
   The folder also keeps compileroutput.svg, the master of the Output tab's glyph, which OutputDockFT.dg inlines. */
Define CS_GlyphCompile                   for "compile"     // Test Compile's run button - amber, keeps its colours
Define CS_GlyphAnalyze                   for "analyze"     // a page under a magnifier - Test Compile's Analyze
Define CS_GlyphModernize                 for "modernize"   // two bent arrows - the editor's Show Compile pane until 2026-10-12; nothing draws it now
Define CS_GlyphCompilePane               for "compilepane" // a window with a pane along its foot - the editor's Show Compile pane, as the class
                                                           // ftg-compilepane; a copy of Bitmaps\CompilePane.svg, the toolbar item's own artwork
Define CS_GlyphToggle                    for "toggle"      // a switch - the analyzer's Toggle Explain
Define CS_GlyphManual                    for "manual"      // an open hand - the Manual Dashboard; traced from Bitmaps\Dk\Manual.ico,
                                                           // the toolbar button's own artwork, so the Start Center lane matches it

/* THE THIRD-PARTY LINKS on the Program Settings dialog, as complete anchors.

   A constant rather than a builder because these live in BOTH twins - ProgramSetup.dg for the
   plain build and ProgramSetupFT.dg for FlexTron - and the plain one must not reach into an FT
   package. RefactorConstants is Used by every program, so it is the one place both can share.

   That sharing is the point: four URLs written out twice each is four chances to update one twin
   and not the other, with nothing to notice until a user clicks a dead link. cLinkLabel takes the
   whole anchor as its Label, so the constant holds the whole anchor. */
Define CS_LinkStarzen            for '<A href="http://www.starzen.com/products/dataflex-tools/dataflex-source-code-browser">Starzen.com</A>'
Define CS_LinkBeyondCompare      for '<A href="http://www.scootersoftware.com">Beyond Compare</A>'
Define CS_LinkWinMerge           for '<A href="http://www.winmerge.org">WinMerge</A>'
Define CS_LinkAraxisMerge        for '<A href="http://www.araxis.com/merge">Araxis Merge</A>'
