// The guarded SELECT-macro definition line DefineSelectMacro splices into modernised files (the indented
// #Replace inside an #IFNDEF SELECT / #ENDIF block). The '!C' part is built from Character() codes on PURPOSE:
// |!C is a DataFlex compile-time auto-increment COUNTER, so a literal "|!C" in our OWN source would be
// evaluated here (to "|17", "|18", ...) instead of stored as text. Building "!" + "C" via Character keeps the
// counter out of DFRefactor's compilation while the WRITTEN output still carries the real |!C for the target
// to evaluate. (124='|' is fine literal - only !C triggers the counter.)
Define CS_SelectMacroDefineLine for ("    #Replace SELECT |" + Character(33) + Character(67))
